# Markdown Style

Follow `docs/conventions/markdown-style.md`. Editor checks come from markdownlint
(`.markdownlint.json`).

- Tables use **compact** style: `| Choice | Value |` with delimiter `| --- | --- |`.
  Never use tight delimiters (`|---|---|`) with spaced cells (MD060).
- One blank line before and after headings, fenced code, lists (when adjacent to other
  content), and tables (MD022 / MD031 / MD032 / MD058).
- ATX headings only; one `#` title per file; do not skip heading levels.
- Fenced code always has a language tag (`python`, `bash`, `sql`, `text`, …) (MD040).
- No trailing spaces; no consecutive blank lines; file ends with one newline.
- Line length is not enforced (MD013 off). Prefer readable breaks, not hard wraps.

```markdown
<!-- ❌ BAD -->
| Choice | Value |
|---|---|
| Language | Python 3.12 |

<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
| Choice | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Language | Python 3.12 |
```

Full reference: `docs/conventions/markdown-style.md`.
